  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn [#commit-a-navigate-event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event), step 7.2 in e.g the [\"reload case\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate-event-firing:update-the-navigation-api-entries-for-a-same-document-navigation), but really also `\"push\"` and `\"replace\"`, we will synchronously fire `oncurrententrychange`. This could result in that the navigate event is aborted, but since we fall through to call intercept handlers we'll end up running those, even though the event is aborted. This leads to `onnavigatesucces` to be fired for an aborted event.",
